\[c=e^{-rT}n(d_{2})\sigma\sqrt{T}+e^{-rT}\left[\ln(S/X)+(b-\sigma^{2}/2)T \right]N(d_{2}), \tag{4.16}\]

where \(N(\cdot)\) is the cumulative normal distribution function, \(n(\cdot)\) is the normal density function, and

\[d_{2}=\frac{\ln(S/X)+(b-\sigma^{2}/2)T}{\sigma\sqrt{T}}\]

