#### Comments

The Hull and White (1988) is a great model to play around with to get some intuition on how stochastic volatility can affect option values. The closed-form approximation is not used much in practice, however, as there are several limits to what values of parameters it accepts. Moreover it is not a very robust approximation, and for some input parameters, the model can even return negative option values.

