The SABR model (Stochastic, \(\alpha\), \(\beta\), \(\rho\) model) published by Hagan, Kumar, Lesniewski, and Woodward (2002) is an interesting model from an option trader's perspective. The Black-76 model has for years been the benchmark model for most European options on currency, interest rates, and stock indices, as well as on commodity and energy futures. The main drawback of the Black-76 (Black-Scholes-Merton) model has been the assumption of constant volatility, or at best a deterministic time varying volatility. Traders have naturally been aware 

