### 10.3 The Milltersen-Schwartz Model

Miltersen and Schwartz (1998) developed an advanced model for pricing options on commodity futures. The model is a three-factor model with stochastic futures price, a term structure of convenience yields,2 and interest rates.3 The model assumes commodity prices are lognormally distributed and that continuously compounded forward interest rates and future convenience yields are normally distributed (aka Gaussian).

